    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test \u2014 the only concrete test class; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe salutation rule composes `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given. I kept structural impact low by putting the branching logic in a fresh, dependency-free helper and letting MapStruct auto-wire the derived field (the same way the existing `initials`/`getInitials()` pair works), so I touched no method inside the large mapper or controller classes.\n\nFive files, each edit small and cohesive:\n\n1. **`Salutations.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny `final` helper mirroring the existing `CustomerCodes`/`MembershipLevels` pattern; holds the only conditional (`compose`).\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` field, its getter/setter, and a one-line `getSalutation()` that delegates to `Salutations.compose(...)`. MapStruct auto-maps `salutation` from this getter and `title` from the setter \u2014 no mapper edits.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (input) to `OwnerFields` and read-only `salutation` to `Owner`, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` carry the fields.\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `title` column (appended at the end, matching the repo's convention of maintaining only the hsqldb/test schema \u2014 the h2/mysql/postgres schemas were already behind on other columns).\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended `NULL` to the ten positional owner seed inserts so their column count matches.\n\nTitle is persisted as a real column (not `@Transient`), so the derived salutation is correct across separate POST/GET transactions in production, not just inside the test's shared transaction.",
